 721                             ; send the last byte unless it is paired up with another to fill the 16-bit
 722                             ; pathway.  If a solution is implemented, it will be done by the host when it
 723                             ; creates the last scatter gather entry in the list.  The command should
 724                             ; contain the actual byte count (an odd value, otherwise it's no problem) but
 725                             ; the last scatter gather entry should have one added to it so an even number
 726                             ; of bytes are "sent" to the target.  The target will dutifully ignore the
 727                             ; extra eight bits since it knows they aren't part of the command.  Failure
 728                             ; to pad with an extra byte would make the 720 hang waiting for the target to
 729                             ; phase change while the target is waiting for the last byte.
