1215                             ; add32:  32-bit addition.  scratcha += scratchb
1216                             ; Usage:
1217                             ;      call add32
1218                             ;
1219                             ; Input:
1220                             ;      32-bits of scratchb
1221                             ;      32-bits of scratcha
1222                             ;
1223                             ; Output:
1224                             ;      32-bits of scratcha, the carry bit contains any overflow
1225                             ;
1226                             ; Returns:
1227                             ;      The carry bit has any overflow generated from the addition
1228                             ;
1229                             ; Uses:
1230                             ;      scratchb is destroyed.
1231                             ;
1232                             ; Desc:
1233                             ;      This operation is surprisingly difficult with the NCR instruction
1234                             ;      set and probably represents a major departure between NCR's intended
1235                             ;      use of the chip and Intel's requirements.
1236                             ;
1237                             ; Algorithm:
1238                             ;      Uses the "register to register move" instruction (an 8-bit move)
1239                             ;      which includes an obscure ability to add an 8-bit value.  The 8-bit
1240                             ;      value must be a constant coded into the "move" instruction.  32-bit
1241                             ;      addition requires 4 additions plus dealing with byte to byte carrys.
1242                             ;
1243                             ;      Move the 4 bytes of scratchb into the 4 instructions where +XXX
1244                             ;      appears.  +XXX is a place holder to (a) persuade the assembler to
1245                             ;      generate the right opcode and (b) provide a visual pattern in a hex
1246                             ;      dump to be sure the right place is modified.
1247                             ;
1248                             ;      Complication!  The move memory instruction is the only mechanism the
1249                             ;      NCR chip provides usable for modifying instructions.  Unfortunately,
1250                             ;      it demands the source and destination be the same number of bytes
1251                             ;      past the last 4-byte boundary.  That is, the source and destination
1252                             ;      address must have the same least significant 2 bits.  (If they are
1253                             ;      not, an "illegal instruction exception occurs.)  As the destination
1254                             ;      is always byte 1 of an instruction, scratchb1 is the only register
1255                             ;      aligned correctly.
1256                             
